From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Close the connections to a database that can't be
 used any more

"Close a database connection" with the forced flag ran only when a
global went away, which fires no events. The specification also has the
user agent force the close "in exceptional circumstances, for example due
to loss of access to the file system", and then fire close at the
connection once its transactions have aborted. Servo had no such case: a
corrupt database failed each transaction with an error, and its
connections stayed open on it.

The executors' errors for a damaged database file (SQLITE_CORRUPT and
SQLITE_NOTADB, RDB_E_SQLITE_CORRUPT) now become BackendError::Unusable,
which fails the request or commit like any other error, and also marks
the engine unusable (KvsEngine::is_unusable). After every batch and
every finished transaction, the manager checks it and closes each open
connection to such a database: it sets the close pending flag and sends
ConnectionEvent::ForcedClose on the connection's result channel. Script
then runs the rest of "close a database connection" with the forced flag:
it aborts the connection's transactions with an AbortError and fires
close at the connection after their abort events. A window in the
back/forward cache is evicted instead, as for versionchange. Once its
connections are closed, the next open of the database opens it anew,
and a delete deletes it. Full disks keep failing only the transaction
(QuotaExceeded).

A connection whose forced close can't be sent, as its global is gone, is
closed as a connection of a gone global, with its transactions rolled
back and finished, so it doesn't hold the next open back (P5 review S2).

Validation: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits`: 151 passed, 1 skipped (new test_corrupt_database_makes_the_engine_unusable, both a plain and a corrupt injected failure); `./mach check --ohos -p servo-storage --all-targets` with SQLite, RDB and both: no warnings; with a temporary hook that marked a database unusable on a page's put (not committed, P5.2/wip/zz-force-close-probe.html), two connections got, in order: the put's error and the writer's abort, the other connection's reader aborted with AbortError, close at both connections (bubbles and cancelable false), transaction() then threw InvalidStateError, and a new open read the stored record (2 of 2 runs, host SM); host IndexedDB/ 4,484 of 4,511 on SM and on QuickJS without unexpected results, /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 312 of 312 SM, 310 of 312 QuickJS (interface lists, as before); after the P5 review fix: host SM release builds, 152 passed, 1 skipped at this commit
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent designed and implemented the forced close in the backend and script, tested it with a temporary fault hook and measured it on both engines; the P5 review fix closes a connection whose forced close can't be sent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
